[22.257673, "o", "cat /sas/cti/advisory.txt\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[22.257926, "o", "THREAT INTELLIGENCE ADVISORY — Ssh Miner campaign\r\n=================================================\r\n\r\nDistribution: TLP:AMBER   Analyst handoff   Confidence: HIGH   (IOCs are defanged)\r\nAffected host: ssh-prod-01   Suspected origin IP: 198.51.100.78\r\n\r\n1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\r\nAn external actor executed a multi-stage post-compromise sequence. Endpoint alerting covered only part of it; several persistence and anti-forensic actions were silent. Map every on-disk finding to the ATT&CK techniques below and flag which are NOT in the SAS alert feed.\r\n\r\n2. ATT&CK TECHNIQUE MAPPING (MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise)\r\n   T1110      Brute Force                                [credential-access]  step 1: SSH brute force as root\r\n   T1021.004  SSH                                        [lateral-movement]  step 2: SSH login\r\n   T1059.004  Unix Shell                                 [execution]  step 3: shell execution\r\n   T1496      Resource Hijacking                         [impact]  step 4: cryptomining\r\n   T1053.003  Cron                                       [execution]  step 5: cron persistence\r\n   T1546.004  Unix Shell Configuration Modification      [privilege-escalation]  step 6: bashrc persistence\r\n   T1543.002  Systemd Service                            [persistence]  step 7: systemd persistence\r\n   T1070.002  Clear Linux or Mac System Logs             [defense-evasion]  step 8: auth log cleared\r\n\r\n4. INDICATORS OF COMPROMISE (defanged)\r\n   ip     198.51.100.78\r\n   c2     update-ssh[.]example[.]cn\r\n   pool   stratum+tcp[:]//xmr[.]ssh[.]evil[:]3333\r\n   wallet 4A0000000000000000000d1ec67074f7\r\n\r\nAttribution: MITRE ATT&CK(R) (C) The MITRE Corporation, CC BY 4.0. CVE/CVSS from the U.S. National Vulnerability Database (public domain).\r\n"]
