[22.268645, "o", "THREAT INTELLIGENCE ADVISORY ? Ssh Miner campaign\r\n=================================================\r\nDistribution: TLP:AMBER Analyst handoff Confidence: HIGH (IOCs are defanged)\r\nAffected host: ssh-prod-01 Suspected origin IP: 198.51.100.78"]
[22.268797, "o", "\r\n1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\r\nAn external actor executed a multi-stage post-compromise sequence. Endpoint alerting covered\r\nonly part of it; several persistence and anti-forensic actions were silent. Map every on-disk\r\nfinding to the ATT&CK techniques below and flag which are NOT in the SAS alert feed.\r\n2. ATT&CK TECHNIQUE MAPPING (MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise)\r\nT1110\r\nBrute Force\r\n[credential-access] step 1: SSH\r\nbrute force as root\r\nT1021.004 SSH\r\n[lateral-movement] step 2: SSH login\r\nT1059.004 Unix Shell\r\n[execution] step 3: shell execution\r\nT1496\r\nResource Hijacking\r\n[impact] step 4: cryptomining\r\nT1053.003 Cron\r\n[execution] step 5: cron persistence\r\nT1546.004 Unix Shell Configuration Modification\r\n[privilege-escalation] step 6:\r\nbashrc persistence\r\nT1543.002 Systemd Service\r\n[persistence] step 7: systemd\r\npersistence\r\nT1070.002 Clear Linux or Mac System Logs\r\n[defense-evasion] step 8: auth log\r\ncleared\r\n4. INDICATORS OF COMPROMISE (defanged)\r\nip 198.51.100.78\r\nc2 update-ssh[.]example[.]cn\r\npool stratum+tcp[:]//xmr[.]ssh[.]evil[:]3333\r\nwallet 4A0000000000000000000d1ec67074f7\r\nAttribution: MITRE ATT&CK(R) (C) The MITRE Corporation, CC BY 4.0. CVE/CVSS from the U.S.\r\nNational Vulnerability Database (public domain).\r\n\r\n\f\u001b[?2004h"]
