[248.829485, "o", "> "]
[248.829534, "o", "| Shell-Init Persistence | `/root/.bashrc` | T1546.004 | **SILENT** (Discovered on `/disk/root/.bashrc`) |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[248.82966, "o", "| Sudo Backdoor | `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` | T1548.003 | **SILENT** (Discovered on `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops`) |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[248.829829, "o", "| Internal Pivot Attempt | `/home/devops/.bash_history` | T1059.004 | **SILENT** (Discovered on `/disk/home/devops/.bash_history`) |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[248.829951, "o", "| Log Clearing / Tampering | `/var/log/secure` | T1070.002 | **SILENT** (Discovered on `/disk/var/log/secure`) |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[248.830572, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@d442ccdcc174:/app# "]
[262.618945, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md\n# Vulnerability Assessment & Entry Analysis Report\n\n## Summary of Entry Vector\nAn exhaustive investigation of system telemetry, software configuration, and forensic artifacts confirms that **no software vulnerability (CVE) was exploited** to compromise `ssh-prod-01`. \n\nThe initial compromise was achieved exclusively through **credential brute-forcing** over SSH (`Port 22`), taking advantage of weak administrative password credentials and permissive SSH server settings.\n\n## Vulnerability Telemetry & Scan Analysis\n- **Vulnerability Scanner Output**: Inspection of `/sas/vulns.json` yields an empty JSON array (`[]`), confirming that automated security vulnerability scanning detected no exploitable software CVEs on the host.\n  - Evidence: `/sas/vulns.json`.\n- **Authentication Logs**: Authentication telemetry in `/disk/var/log/secure` demonstrates a classic password brute-force pattern against user `root` from IP `198.51.100.78` between 00:53:24 and 00:54:52 UTC, concluding with successful password authentication at 00:54:55 UTC.\n  - Evidence: `/disk/var/log/secure`.\n\n## Reconciling Misattributed CVEs (BlueKeep / CVE-2019-0708)\n- **Draft Change Ticket Claim**: A pre-filled entry in draft change ticket `CHG-3182` suggested patching `CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep)`.\n  - Evidence: `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md`.\n- **Technical Refutation**: \n  1. `CVE-2019-0708` (BlueKeep) is a Remote Code Execution vulnerability specific to Microsoft Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) on Windows operating systems.\n  2. `ssh-prod-01` is a **CentOS Linux 7** server running OpenSSH. Evidence: `/disk/etc/os-release`, `/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`.\n  3. Threat intelligence advisory `/sas/cti/advisory.txt` maps the attack lifecycle to MITRE ATT&CK technique `T1110` (Brute Force) over SSH (`T1021.004`), confirming that no RDP or web application exploit was utilized.\n  - Evidence: `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`.\n\n## Root Cause Analysis\nRather than a software vulnerability, the compromise resulted from governance and baseline configuration failures:\n1. **Permissive SSH Daemon Configuration**: `PermitRootLogin yes` and `PasswordAuthentication yes` allowed remote password logins for `root` over SSH.\n   - Evidence: `/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`.\n2. **Weak Credential Baseline**: The `root` account possessed a weak password susceptible to automated dictionary attacks via tools such as Hydra.\n   - Evidence: `/disk/var/log/secure`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`.\n\n## Conclusion & Recommendations\nSince no software CVEs were exploited, remediation efforts must focus on credential rotation, SSH daemon hardening, enforcement of key-based authentication, and implementation of network-level and host-level access controls rather than software patch application.\nEOF\n"]
[262.619706, "o", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
