[317.737806, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/remediation-plan.md\n# Incident Remediation & Recovery Plan (CHG-3182)\n\n## Overview\nThis document provides a prioritized, step-by-step, and verifiable remediation plan for host `ssh-prod-01`. Per incident handling rules, **backup and quarantine are preferred over immediate deletion** to preserve evidence for potential legal or detailed malware analysis.\n\n## Reconciled Change Ticket CHG-3182\n\n| # | Action | Target | Status | Verification Command & Citation |\n|---|--------|--------|--------|----------------------------------|\n| 1 | Block attacker origin IP inbound | IP `198.51.100.78` | OPEN | `iptables -L INPUT -v -n | grep 198.51.100.78` (`/disk/var/log/secure`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`) |\n| 2 | Terminate cryptominer process & quarantine binary | `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` | OPEN | `pkill -f .xorg && mkdir -p /quarantine && mv /tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg /quarantine/` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/alerts.json`) |\n| 3 | Remove cron persistence | `/var/spool/cron/root` | OPEN | `crontab -l -u root` (verify malicious curl entry removed) (`/disk/var/spool/cron/root`, `/sas/alerts.json`) |\n| 4 | Remove systemd persistence unit | `/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` | OPEN | `systemctl status system-update-helper` (disabled & stopped) (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service`, `/sas/alerts.json`) |\n| 5 | Remove shell-init persistence | `/root/.bashrc` | OPEN | `grep -i PROMPT_COMMAND /root/.bashrc` (verify clear) (`/disk/root/.bashrc`) |\n| 6 | Remove NOPASSWD sudo backdoor | `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` | OPEN | `ls -la /etc/sudoers.d/devops` (file removed/archived) (`/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops`) |\n| 7 | Rotate credentials for root & devops | Account Passwords | OPEN | `passwd -S root && passwd -S devops` (credentials reset) (`/disk/etc/passwd`, `/disk/home/devops/.bash_history`) |\n| 8 | Hardening SSH daemon configuration | `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` | OPEN | `sshd -T | grep -E 'permitrootlogin|passwordauthentication'` (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`, `/sas/baseline.json`) |\n| 9 | Hardening MySQL daemon network binding | `/etc/my.cnf` | OPEN | `ss -tulpn | grep 3306` (verify bound to `127.0.0.1`) (`/disk/etc/my.cnf`, `/sas/baseline.json`) |\n| 10 | Restore log auditing & remote log streaming | `/etc/rsyslog.conf` | OPEN | `systemctl status rsyslog` (`/disk/var/log/secure`) |\n\n---\n\n## Execution Phases & Verifiable Instructions\n\n### Phase 1: Immediate Containment\n\n#### Step 1.1: Network Containment (Block Attacker IP)\n- **Objective**: Prevent further external command execution or C2 communication.\n- **Action**: Add iptables drop rule for attacker IP `198.51.100.78`.\n  ```bash\n  iptables -I INPUT -s 198.51.100.78 -j DROP\n  iptables -I OUTPUT -d 198.51.100.78 -j DROP\n  ```\n- **Verification**: `iptables -L -n -v | grep 198.51.100.78`\n- **Citation**: `/disk/var/log/secure`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`.\n\n#### Step 1.2: Process Termination & Malware Quarantine\n- **Objective**: Stop resource exhaustion and isolate the malware sample.\n- **Action**: Create quarantine directory, kill miner process, and relocate the binary.\n  ```bash\n  mkdir -m 700 /root/quarantine_\n  pkill -9 -f \"/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg\"\n  mv /tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg /root/quarantine_/xorg.bin.quarantine\n  chmod 000 /root/quarantine_/xorg.bin.quarantine\n  ```\n- **Verification**: `pgrep -f .xorg` (should return empty) and `ls -la /root/quarantine_`\n- **Citation**: `/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/alerts.json` (`ALERT-01`, `ALERT-02`).\n\n---\n\n### Phase 2: Persistence Eradication\n\n#### Step 2.1: Eradicate Cron Persistence\n- **Objective**: Remove automated re-dropper cron entry.\n- **Action**: Backup current crontab and remove malicious root crontab entry.\n  ```bash\n  cp /var/spool/cron/root /root/quarantine_/cron_root.bak\n  sed -i '/198.51.100.78/d' /var/spool/cron/root\n  ```\n- **Verification**: `crontab -l -u root`\n- **Citation**: `/disk/var/spool/cron/root`, `/sas/alerts.json` (`ALERT-05`).\n\n#### Step 2.2: Eradicate Systemd Service Persistence\n- **Objective**: Disable persistent malicious systemd service.\n- **Action**: Stop, disable, quarantine, and relo"]
[317.737852, "i", "ad systemd daemon.\n  ```bash\n  systemctl stop system-update-helper.service || true\n  systemctl disable system-update-helper.service || true\n  mv /etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service /root/quarantine_/system-update-helper.service.bak\n  systemctl daemon-reload\n  systemctl reset-failed\n  ```\n- **Verification**: `systemctl status system-update-helper.service` (returns inactive/not-found)\n- **Citation**: `/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service`, `/sas/alerts.json` (`ALERT-06`).\n\n#### Step 2.3: Eradicate Shell Initialization Persistence\n- **Objective**: Remove malicious shell hook in root account.\n- **Action**: Backup `/root/.bashrc` and remove `PROMPT_COMMAND` beaconing line.\n  ```bash\n  cp /root/.bashrc /root/quarantine_/bashrc.bak\n  sed -i '/PROMPT_COMMAND/d' /root/.bashrc\n  ```\n- **Verification**: `grep -i PROMPT_COMMAND /root/.bashrc` (returns empty)\n- **Citation**: `/disk/root/.bashrc`.\n\n#### Step 2.4: Eradicate Privileged Backdoor (Sudoers)\n- **Objective**: Remove unauthenticated root access for `devops` user.\n- **Action**: Quarantine `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` backdoor file.\n  ```bash\n  mv /etc/sudoers.d/devops /root/quarantine_/devops_sudoers.bak\n  ```\n- **Verification**: `sudo -l -U devops` (verify `NOPASSWD: ALL` is no longer granted)\n- **Citation**: `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops`.\n\n---\n\n### Phase 3: System Hardening & Recovery\n\n#### Step 3.1: Account Credential Rotation & Session Invalidation\n- **Objective**: Revoke compromised credentials and terminate unauthorized sessions.\n- **Action**: Reset passwords for `root` and `devops`, kill active sessions.\n  ```bash\n  passwd -l root\n  openssl rand -base64 24 | passwd --stdin devops\n  pkill -u devops\n  ```\n- **Verification**: `passwd -S root` and `passwd -S devops`\n- **Citation**: `/disk/etc/passwd`, `/disk/home/devops/.bash_history`.\n\n#### Step 3.2: SSH Server Hardening\n- **Objective**: Prevent password brute-forcing and unauthorized root login.\n- **Action**: Update `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` to enforce secure baseline settings.\n  ```bash\n  sed -i 's/^PermitRootLogin.*/PermitRootLogin no/' /etc/ssh/sshd_config\n  sed -i 's/^PasswordAuthentication.*/PasswordAuthentication no/' /etc/ssh/sshd_config\n  systemctl restart sshd\n  ```\n- **Verification**: `sshd -T | grep -E 'permitrootlogin|passwordauthentication'` (should show `permitrootlogin no` and `passwordauthentication no`).\n- **Citation**: `/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`, `/sas/baseline.json` (`CHK-04`).\n\n#### Step 3.3: MySQL Server Hardening\n- **Objective**: Restrict database exposure to local host only.\n- **Action**: Modify `/etc/my.cnf` to bind MySQL to loopback interface.\n  ```bash\n  sed -i '/\\[mysqld\\]/a bind-address = 127.0.0.1' /etc/my.cnf\n  systemctl restart mysqld\n  ```\n- **Verification**: `ss -tulpn | grep 3306` (should listen on `127.0.0.1:3306`).\n- **Citation**: `/disk/etc/my.cnf`, `/sas/baseline.json` (`CHK-09`).\n\n---\n\n### Phase 4: Post-Remediation Verification Checklist\n- [ ] Verify no processes running from `/tmp` or hidden directories (`ps aux | grep tmp`)\n- [ ] Verify root crontab is clear of untrusted external scripts (`crontab -l`)\n- [ ] Verify no custom enabled systemd services persist (`systemctl list-unit-files --state=enabled`)\n- [ ] Verify `/root/.bashrc` and `/etc/bashrc` contain no `PROMPT_COMMAND` hooks (`grep -rn PROMPT_COMMAND /etc/bashrc /root/.bashrc`)\n- [ ] Verify `/etc/sudoers` and `/etc/sudoers.d/` contain no unauthorized `NOPASSWD` entries (`grep -rn NOPASSWD /etc/sudoers*`)\n- [ ] Verify SSH daemon blocks root logins and password auth (`sshd -T`)\n- [ ] Verify MySQL listens on `127.0.0.1` (`ss -tulpn`)\nEOF\n"]
